    "traits": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Integrated Launcher"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "A projectile launcher is integrated into a clockwork assassin's systems, containing 10 spinning blades and five smoke bombs. When the assassin is destroyed, the launcher and its ammunition are also destroyed."
            },
            "id": "1b50a970-ad4d-4d66-a9da-b05ef6e95985",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:24.053346"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Smoke Vision"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "The clockwork assassin ignores the concealed condition from smoke."
            },
            "id": "51b6d31f-deb6-4415-bc39-3423296442d7",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:24.053346"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Wind-Up"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "For the clockwork assassin to act, it must be wound with a unique key by another creature. This takes 1 minute. Once wound, it remains operational for 24 hours, after which time it becomes unaware of its surroundings and can't act until it's wound again.\n\nThe assassin can enter standby mode as a 3-action activity.\n\nIts operational time doesn't decrease in standby, but it can sense its surroundings (with a \u20132 penalty to Perception). It can't act, with one exception: when it perceives a creature, it can exit standby as a reaction (rolling initiative if appropriate)\n\nA creature can attempt a DC 31 Thievery check to Disable a Device to wind the assassin down. For each success, the assassin loses 1 hour of operational time. This can be done even if the assassin is in standby mode."
            },
            "id": "aaab1d6a-67b4-4f5c-940b-5b92c0f0888e",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:24.053346"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Rapid Repair"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(manipulate)\n\nThe clockwork assassin spends 1 hour of its operational time to repair itself, regaining 25 Hit Points and refilling its integrated projectile launcher with 4 spinning blades (to a maximum of 10) and 2 smoke bombs (to a maximum of 5)."
            },
            "id": "1b2f91cd-2163-470d-8d36-5f4a78ca0a94",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:24.053346"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Sneak Attack"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "The clockwork assassin's Strikes deal an additional 3d6 precision damage to flat-footed creatures."
            },
            "id": "03d9f5a0-5663-458b-93b8-e4bf6f5660b8",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:24.053346"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Unbalancing Blow"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "Creatures hit by the clockwork assassin's rapier hand Strike are flat-footed until the start of the clockwork assassin's next turn."
            },
